WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.100
It's Friday, November 27, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.670
Who gets a seat at the table?

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.580
Nvidia has reportedly stopped shipping AI servers to four Southeast Asian countries.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.930
Dell and Supermicro have reportedly told buyers their orders can't ship.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.640
Washington wants top chips kept away from China,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.540
and Chinese labs are feeling it.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.210
Z.ai's next big model is reportedly late.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.330
Moonshot's gap between big releases could double, to a year.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.860
In Korea, the AI memory chip boom has growth beating forecasts,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.970
so the central bank raised rates.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.090
Oh, and Nvidia's boss is back,

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:59.100
so Denny's put his plaque back up. His booth is waiting.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.070
Now, the money.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:05.910
Elon Musk says every child in America is getting two SpaceX shares.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:13.270
One from SpaceX next month, one from Musk in June. That's about $18 billion.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:20.190
Dell, meanwhile, has a record $132 billion of AI server orders still to fill.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:27.740
Its AI server sales nearly quadrupled in a year, to $22 billion in one quarter.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.120
Neuralink just got FDA approval for America's first pivotal trial of a brain implant,

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.390
for people with ALS.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.180
And OpenAI says it's proved the speed limit for multiplying grids of numbers,

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.550
the math inside almost every computer.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.660
The catch?

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.800
Hidden AI use has hit at least 25 court cases in England and Wales this year.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.890
And Swiss officials say hackers used AI agents in five attacks.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.340
Volvo's training humanoid robots at its plant in Ghent.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.740
They learn the job by copying people.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.040
They roll on wheels, carry parts,

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.020
and could join real production from the middle of next year.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.440
And XPeng says its humanoid will cost about the same as an electric car.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.050
This Thanksgiving, don't just ask what the machines can do.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.060
Ask who gets a seat at the table.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.040
Want the whole month? Hear more tonight.
